the invariant of the while loop in 'field-write' is not analysed statically: the loop body assigns through a place expression; both runtime checks kept
the invariant of the while loop in 'early' is not analysed statically: a nested loop in the body can `return`; both runtime checks kept
the invariant of the while loop in 'nested-read' is not analysed statically: 'j' is assigned by a nested loop and read after it; both runtime checks kept
the invariant of the while loop in 'borrowed' is not analysed statically: the loop borrows 'acc'
the invariant of the while loop in 'via-lambda' is not analysed statically: 'i' is borrowed, or assigned inside a lambda or handler clause
the invariant of the while loop in 'via-handler' is not analysed statically: 'acc' is borrowed, or assigned inside a lambda or handler clause
the invariant of the while loop in 'shadowing' is not analysed statically: the loop body's `let` rebinds 'i'
the invariant of the while loop in 'named-borrow' is not analysed statically: 'lim' is borrowed, or assigned inside a lambda or handler clause
the invariant of the while loop in 'borrow-in-loop' is not analysed statically: the loop borrows 'lim', so a call in it could write it
